Z||000000||fierohoho||12-27-2001||04:08 PM||||Has anyone put a turbo on the iron duke in their Fiero?<P>Do you have pics?<P>What power gains did you notice?<P>------------------<BR>'84 SE 2.5l<BR>'85 Coupe 2.5l now getting a 3800<BR>'86 SE 2.5l<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/lightbar.gif"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Standard||12-27-2001||04:56 PM||||hmm... boom!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Stock duke block really isn't strong enough to hold up to any boost.. of course, if you have an extra one to play around with.. hehe  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/quad_sig_pic_1.jpg">        <BR><FONT COLOR="red">1988 Quad 4 Coupe 5 speed</FONT><BR><FONT SIZE="1"><FONT COLOR="white">1986 GT 5 speed, 1984 SC Auto</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="blue">AOL: LastMinuteBastrd  AIM: SavedbyJebus</FONT></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000002||KEV||12-27-2001||07:25 PM||||The block can handle the increase in power, IRM back in the day used to offer a Turbo for the 84-86 4 cyl. Bolt and go.no mod's to the lower half. The power increased from 90hp to about 150hp,not to bad for a duke. GM still offers a Super Duty head for the stock Duke Block, for more power. <P>------------------<BR>BLACK85GT 3800V6 2"DROP, FLUSHMOUNT HEADLIGHTS AND WRAPAROUND WING, 17' WHEELS ON FRONT 18'ON REAR||||reg||1
Z||000003||fieroman_5000||12-27-2001||07:47 PM||||A local GM dealer up here sells the SD block and Head. the SD block goes for :trying to remember exact numbers: $836.86 ... or something like that  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> If you wanted to get 150 HP out of a Duke RELIABLY (key word) you will have to go with SD parts.<P>Fieroman  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by fieroman_5000 (edited 12-27-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||KEV||12-27-2001||08:06 PM||||Well GM doesn't sell SD-4 blocks anymore, you can only get them throught Kansas Racing. And there Around $1000+ for one. You can build up a Duke and make it reliable. I did a Performace Rebuild on my 84 fiero,(cam,lifters,ported and polished head,high comp.pistons,ported intake & TBI,custom header) it makes about 140hp and I've put over 8,000 miles on it and not a problem. <P>------------------<BR>Minnesota Fieros Forever President<BR>1985 Black Gt(3800 V6,Flushmount headlights,Wraparound Wing,Lowered 2",17" on front,18"on rear)||||reg||1
Z||000005||erikred||12-28-2001||02:30 PM||||Yes. Read the archives. <P>Erik-||||reg||1
Z||000006||BV MotorSports||12-28-2001||07:20 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by KEV:<BR><B>Well GM doesn't sell SD-4 blocks anymore, you can only get them throught Kansas Racing. And there Around $1000+ for one. <BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>GM part # <BR>Engine hardware package 10031328<P>SD block 10093306 (KRP 785 922-6644)<P>SD alum head 10049801<P>2.5 alum SD head 10045437<P>Rocker cover 10031327<P>SD timing gears 10037684<P>SD 4bbl intake 10093374<P>Hope this helps...yeah, I work for GM!<BR>Steven<P><P>------------------<BR>87 Fiero GT 14.9/ 89mph<BR>94 Formula WS6 w/ NOS 12.4 /118mph<BR>87 Conquest TSi <BR>87 Conquest TSi 406 SBC V8!<BR>85.5 Starion ESi||||reg||12
Z||000007||BV MotorSports||12-28-2001||07:25 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Standard:<BR><B>hmm... boom!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Stock duke block really isn't strong enough to hold up to any boost.. of course, if you have an extra one to play around with.. hehe   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif"><P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I had a 84 Fiero w/ a turbocharged duke. The kit was made by IRM, Jim Sutter, and was a very nice set-up. It used a Mitsubishi turbo and made 6-8 pounds of boost. Kit made 155hp and was fun! Boy I miss that car. All except for the time it caught on fire.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>Steven<P><P>------------------<BR>87 Fiero GT 14.9/ 89mph<BR>94 Formula WS6 w/ NOS 12.4 /118mph<BR>87 Conquest TSi <BR>87 Conquest TSi 406 SBC V8!<BR>85.5 Starion ESi||||reg||1
